<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 126 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 126 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 126 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.0 BLN    850 MLN    650 MLN    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    450 MLN!   576 MLN!   =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1 BANK BILLS    =	     96 MLN*    26 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 1 T-BILLS	 =	     =	   100 MLN*   =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES) ! INCLUDES 354 MLN STG REPO EXPIRING MARCH 10 AT 5-31/32 PCT</p>
<p>(INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
